    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0184" n="1018" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1018"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/608a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Representatives in Certain Countries
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d119-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-21T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Before sending recommendations for the addition of names to the enemy trading
                    list or for removals therefrom, confer with the British and French diplomatic
                    representatives in the country to which you are accredited. Such action will
                    further our purposes of common counsel and cooperation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d119-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d119-f1-content">
                <p>Those in Central and South America and in Norway, Sweden, Denmar the Netherlands,
                    Spain, and Switzerland.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
